## 4. Win7 API-set compatibility shims

| | |
|---|---|
| Components | `ai/win7/*.dll` — 4 `w7shim-*.dll` and 20 `api-ms-win-core-*.dll` |
| Copyright | See individual files; these are Microsoft-authored API-set forwarders |
| License | MIT (redistributed as part of the ONNX Runtime Win7 support scheme) |
| Why bundled | Windows 7 does not ship the Universal C Runtime API sets that ONNX Runtime 1.14 imports. These files satisfy those imports on Win7 without changing the runtime itself. |

The 4 `w7shim-*.dll` are the actual patch: the import table of
`ai/win7/onnxruntime.dll` was rewritten so that the four API sets absent from
Windows 7 are imported under ordinary filenames instead. The Windows loader
resolves `api-ms-win-*` through a built-in API-set schema and never consults
the filesystem, so a same-named DLL placed alongside the binary would be
ignored; renaming the import is what forces a filesystem lookup.

The 20 `api-ms-win-core-*.dll` serve a different purpose: they are fallback
copies for the API-set entries Windows 7's own API-set coverage does not
provide. On Windows 8 and later they are redundant, because the system schema
resolves those names directly — `tools/ProbeShim.cs` demonstrates the patched
runtime loading without them. On Windows 7 they are the only thing that can
satisfy those imports, so they must ship in the same directory as the patched
runtime.

Nothing here is linked by Restoria's own code; no AI code path runs in the
main process.

